      "output": {
        "decision": "answer",
        "reason": "The resolved question is fully supported by the supplied evidence from paper 1805.11598: (1) combined resources are training data and multilingual word vectors across CoNLL 2009 languages, with supervision from English added to monolingual parsers (c-ab37506cf0e270f6ab4a5722); (2) no parallel data is required (c-8b21bd8c4c41f76753d2758d, c-f04cb29df42fdbc211d852cf); (3) annotation dissimilarity is handled without alignment, using parameter sharing/simple data combination (c-ab37506cf0e270f6ab4a5722, c-f04cb29df42fdbc211d852cf); (4) training is polyglot training of one model on multiple languages with variants such as language ID and language-specific LSTMs (c-ab37506cf0e270f6ab4a5722, c-bb02e8199a80bde6c03e4d79); (5) evaluation is on seven CoNLL 2009 languages, with improvements notable for low-resource languages and little/no gain for Czech and Chinese (c-ab37506cf0e270f6ab4a5722, c-bb02e8199a80bde6c03e4d79). No external knowledge is added."
